# Report which operating mode is live.
#
# Served by syncai_sys_manager on the relative name `get_mode`, so it lands on
# <robot_id>/get_mode.
#
# The answer is DERIVED, not remembered: it comes from asking byobu which
# session actually exists. That way it stays correct across a sys_manager
# restart, and it cannot drift from reality if someone builds or kills a session
# by hand.
#
# mode values are defined as constants in RobotMode (MAINTENANCE/MANUAL/AUTO).
# MAINTENANCE means no session is running at all — the stack is down.
#
# success is false only when the answer is ambiguous, i.e. both the navigation
# and mapping sessions exist at once (possible only if they were built by hand;
# switch_mode always kills every known session before building one). `mode` then
# holds the first match and `message` names both.
#
# session is the byobu session name backing the reported mode, empty in
# MAINTENANCE. Useful for `byobu attach -t <session>`.
---
bool success
string message
uint8 mode
string session
